{
    "background_story": "Ryder, a former soldier, had seen his fair share of battles. But it was the infliction of a severe injury during his last tour that changed his life forever. A roadside bomb had left him with a permanent limp and a deep emotional scar. Struggling to cope with the physical and mental pain, Ryder turned to extreme sports as a way to channel his emotions. He became a professional cage fighter, using the adrenaline rush to mask the anguish. However, as time passed, Ryder realized that the infliction of pain on himself and others wasn't the answer. He began to focus on his recovery, using his experience to help others who were struggling with similar traumas. Ryder's story became one of redemption, as he transformed from a vessel of pain to a beacon of hope for those affected by infliction.",
